    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="2" relname="preparation">Good that you presented the ISO 9241 definition of usability.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="10" relname="span">It's been around for a while</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="9" relname="span">and it's good that it is included in ISO standards.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="8" relname="span">We still have a way to go, however, in really breaking down usability attributes into measurable units.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="6" relname="concession">Some strides have been made with this,</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="11" relname="span">but more refinement is needed.</segment>
        <group id="7" type="span"/>
        <group id="8" type="span" parent="7" relname="span"/>
        <group id="9" type="span" parent="4" relname="concession"/>
        <group id="10" type="span" parent="3" relname="circumstance"/>
        <group id="11" type="span" parent="8" relname="summary"/>
    </body>
</rst>
